<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons for Arcane Mage DPS Phase 4</h2>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-and-two-handed-weapons-for-arcane-mage-dps-phase-4">Main-Hand and Two-Handed Weapons for Arcane Mage DPS Phase 4</h4>This is by far the slot with the most power creep, the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a> weapons are just far better than anything else available. The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50732/bloodsurge-kelthuzads-blade-of-agony">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_150.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodsurge, Kel'Thuzad's Blade of Agony</span></a> is the baseline main choice and will be best in slot for anyone who can use a sword. Alternatively the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50731/archus-greatstaff-of-antonidas">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_108.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Archus, Greatstaff of Antonidas</span></a> drops from the same boss, but is over 120 dps worse. <br/>
<br/>Past those two, every item is several hundred dps worse, with the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50704/rigormortis">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_152.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigormortis</span></a> as third best, gapped by 240 dps by the best in slot weapon. Right after that, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50608/frozen-bonespike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_101.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frozen Bonespike</span></a> is closer to a 290 dps difference. There's also the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50725/dying-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_106.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dying Light</span></a> staff, which although nothing amazing, can be a solid upgrade since it's only 340 dps from best in slot, and it's from an earlier boss in the raid which if you obtain can help with progression in harder bosses.<br/>
<br/>Again from the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a>, but this time from 10-Man, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51939/telthas-dagger-of-the-blood-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_101.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tel'thas, Dagger of the Blood King</span></a> is the 5th best weapon, at 300 dps from its 25-man counterpart. While the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51943/halion-staff-of-forgotten-love">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_109.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Halion, Staff of Forgotten Love</span></a> two-handed weapon is nearly at 390 dps from the best in slot sword, and 270 dps from it's staff counterpart from 25-Man. <br/>
<br/>Meanwhile, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50648/nibelung">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_109.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nibelung</span></a> is a very unique item, where a lot of its power comes not from stats, but from the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71844/summon-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_svalasorrowgrave.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Summon Val'kyr</span></a> passive it has, this is sadly not amazing for arcane as it doesn't have many debuff applications which can instead how many summons you have at one time unlike fire, but it's still a solid upgrade from a relatively early raid boss. Though if possible, try to pass this to a class that does benefit more from the passive such as a fire mage or balance druid, since it's not only great but near best in slot for them situationally.<br/>
<br/>From the other bosses in 10-Man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51932/frost-needle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_152.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Needle</span></a> is over 500 dps worse than the best weapon, but you should grab it as soon as you can if given the option, since it's a really good upgrade from last phase's best in slot weapons. The same applies to the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51815/bleak-coldarra-carver">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_101.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bleak Coldarra Carver</span></a> which is 50 dps worse than the previously mentioned sword. There's also the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51898/maghari-chieftains-staff">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_107.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mag'hari Chieftain's Staff</span></a> staff, which is slightly worse than best in slot options from phase 3, but if you don't have a good off-hand it's more than likely an upgrade as a whole.<br/>
<br/>From last phase, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47518/mortalis">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_137.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mortalis</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47422/barb-of-tarasque">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Barb of Tarasque</span></a> perform similarly, and which one you use or pick depends on your hit situation. While the phase 2 best in slot <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45620/starshard-edge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Starshard Edge</span></a> fell off in performance due to the lack of secondary stats, over 200 dps worse than the two previously mentioned weapons.<br/>
<br/>If you can afford it, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50047/queldelar-lens-of-the-mind">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_155.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quel'Delar, Lens of the Mind</span></a> can be obtained outside of raids, either by having it drop in one of your dungeon runs, or getting it from the auction house through the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50380/battered-hilt">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qiraj_hiltornate.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Battered Hilt</span></a> quests. Otherwise, there's now the 245 ilvl version of the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47422/barb-of-tarasque">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Barb of Tarasque</span></a> from 25-Man Normal, which is now obtainable from a vendor through the new currency you can obtain in the Heroic Gamma dungeons. This should be the bare minimum weapon to enter <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>.<div class="quote-box" data-has-source="false" data-type="user">
<div class="quote-header"></div>
